  "type": "singleCorrect",
  "level": 2,
  "question": {
    "text": "A ball is released from a height <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>h</mi></math>. If <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math> be the time required to complete first half and second half of the distance respectively. Then, choose the correct relation between <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math>.",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "lBvcq",
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mfenced><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt></mfenced><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math>",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "4k40d",
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mfenced><mrow><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math>",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "JDCwS",
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mfenced><mrow><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></math>",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "kOThO",
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mfenced><mrow><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></math>",
      "isCorrect": true,
      "image": null
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p>As the body is dropped from a certain height&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>h</mi></math>, its initial velocity will be zero.</p><p>For first half,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>h</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>h</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math>.</p><p>Using second equation of motion,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>s</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>u</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mi>a</mi><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math></p><p>We have,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mi>h</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mi>g</mi><msubsup><mi>t</mi><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></math>.</p><p>Time taken in travel first half of the height,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mfrac><mi>h</mi><mi>g</mi></mfrac></msqrt><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mfenced><mn>1</mn></mfenced></math>.</p><p>For total height <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>h</mi></math>, using again second equation of motion,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>h</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mi>g</mi><msup><mfenced><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>&#8658;</mo><mfenced><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>h</mi></mrow><mi>g</mi></mfrac></msqrt><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mfenced><mn>2</mn></mfenced></math></p><p>From equation&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mn>1</mn></mfenced></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mn>2</mn></mfenced></math>,&nbsp;</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mfrac><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></math></p><p>Thus, the relation is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mfenced><mrow><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></math>.</p></blockquote>",
